1
00:00:05,000 --> 00:00:08,000
[narrator] In the Dentora region
of the Republic of Padokea,

2
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:11,000
there is a dormant volcano
surrounded by forests

3
00:00:11,000 --> 00:00:14,000
measuring 3722 meters high

4
00:00:14,000 --> 00:00:16,000
called Kukuroo Mountain.

5
00:00:16,000 --> 00:00:20,000
It is home to a family
of famous assassins:

6
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:21,000
The Zoldyck family.

7
00:00:23,000 --> 00:00:27,000
Visitors arrive every day in hopes
of catching a glimpse of the mansion,

8
00:00:27,000 --> 00:00:29,000
which has never been seen.

9
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:33,000
It’s one of this nation’s
most popular tourist attractions.

10
00:00:33,000 --> 00:00:35,000
LAMENTATION TOURS

11
00:00:41,000 --> 00:00:43,000
[theme song playing]

12
00:01:56,000 --> 00:01:57,000
Very well.

13
00:01:58,000 --> 00:02:00,000
You’re free to go now.

14
00:02:00,000 --> 00:02:01,000
But, Kil…

15
00:02:05,000 --> 00:02:06,000
Promise me one thing…

16
00:02:08,000 --> 00:02:10,000
That you will never betray your friends.

17
00:02:11,000 --> 00:02:12,000
Got that?

18
00:02:15,000 --> 00:02:17,000
I’ll never betray them.

19
00:02:19,000 --> 00:02:20,000
I swear.

20
00:02:20,000 --> 00:02:25,000
CAN'T SEE x IF x YOU'RE BLIND

21
00:02:29,000 --> 00:02:32,000
[narrator] After speaking with his father,
whom he greatly admires,

22
00:02:32,000 --> 00:02:34,000
Killua leaves home once again,

23
00:02:34,000 --> 00:02:36,000
despite his mother’s objections.

24
00:02:38,000 --> 00:02:42,000
Canary leads Gon and his friends
to the butler’s quarters,

25
00:02:42,000 --> 00:02:44,000
in an attempt to meet with Killua.

26
00:02:47,000 --> 00:02:49,000
[tired exhale] Are we there yet?

27
00:02:49,000 --> 00:02:51,000
Still a bit farther.

28
00:02:51,000 --> 00:02:52,000
[Leorio sighs]

29
00:02:52,000 --> 00:02:54,000
But we’ve been walking forever…

30
00:02:57,000 --> 00:03:00,000
[Kikyo] Oh, I am positively furious!

31
00:03:00,000 --> 00:03:02,000
Kil finally came home to us

32
00:03:02,000 --> 00:03:05,000
but my husband’s
allowed him to leave again!

33
00:03:05,000 --> 00:03:07,000
And Father is just as guilty,

34
00:03:07,000 --> 00:03:09,000
releasing him
without asking my permission!

35
00:03:09,000 --> 00:03:12,000
Honestly! Every single time!

36
00:03:12,000 --> 00:03:15,000
They all just act
without consulting me first!

37
00:03:16,000 --> 00:03:17,000
Understand, Gotoh?

38
00:03:18,000 --> 00:03:19,000
[Gotoh] Yes, ma'am.

39
00:03:20,000 --> 00:03:21,000
[Kikyo sobs]

40
00:03:24,000 --> 00:03:27,000
This... This is
a most critical time for Kil.

41
00:03:28,000 --> 00:03:31,000
Why doesn’t anyone understand?

42
00:03:31,000 --> 00:03:32,000
[sobs lightly]

43
00:03:34,000 --> 00:03:37,000
He’s the one child I shall not give up!

44
00:03:38,000 --> 00:03:40,000
[Kikyo sobbing]

45
00:03:41,000 --> 00:03:42,000
[frogs croaking]

46
00:03:48,000 --> 00:03:49,000
[Canary] There it is.

47
00:03:51,000 --> 00:03:52,000
[Leorio] That’s it, huh?

48
00:03:53,000 --> 00:03:56,000
It’s still a lot farther away
than I’d like.

49
00:03:56,000 --> 00:03:57,000
Hey, Canary.

50
00:03:58,000 --> 00:04:00,000
Aren’t you gonna get
in a lot of trouble with your bosses

51
00:04:00,000 --> 00:04:01,000
for bringing us here?

52
00:04:02,000 --> 00:04:04,000
They are perfectly aware
of what I’m doing.

53
00:04:04,000 --> 00:04:06,000
I am quite certain of that.

54
00:04:07,000 --> 00:04:09,000
I’m prepared for the consequences.

55
00:04:09,000 --> 00:04:11,000
If there’s any trouble,
I’ll take responsibility.

56
00:04:13,000 --> 00:04:18,000
No. I am merely serving as a guide
for Master Killua’s friends.

57
00:04:31,000 --> 00:04:33,000
Master Killua.
We’ve been waiting for you.

58
00:04:34,000 --> 00:04:34,000
Gotoh.

59
00:04:35,000 --> 00:04:36,000
Where is Gon right now?

60
00:04:37,000 --> 00:04:38,000
You know, don’t you?

61
00:04:39,000 --> 00:04:42,000
Canary is bringing Master Gon
along with his two friends,

62
00:04:42,000 --> 00:04:44,000
even as we speak.

63
00:04:45,000 --> 00:04:46,000
Seriously?

64
00:04:46,000 --> 00:04:48,000
They’ll be arriving shortly,

65
00:04:48,000 --> 00:04:49,000
so please wait inside.

66
00:04:50,000 --> 00:04:50,000
Sure.

67
00:04:55,000 --> 00:04:56,000
-Gotoh.
-Sir.

68
00:04:57,000 --> 00:04:58,000
The second he’s here, tell me.

69
00:04:58,000 --> 00:05:01,000
[Gotoh]
Of course. I shall notify you immediately.

70
00:05:10,000 --> 00:05:13,000
Please forgive me Master Killua.

71
00:05:19,000 --> 00:05:21,000
[Leorio] We finally made it!

72
00:05:30,000 --> 00:05:31,000
Welcome, gentlemen.

73
00:05:35,000 --> 00:05:38,000
[Gotoh]
We apologize for our previous discourtesy.

74
00:05:39,000 --> 00:05:42,000
We have been informed
by the lady of the house

75
00:05:42,000 --> 00:05:43,000
that from now on

76
00:05:43,000 --> 00:05:46,000
you are to be treated as official guests.

77
00:05:47,000 --> 00:05:49,000
There, does that feel better?

78
00:05:49,000 --> 00:05:50,000
It does! Thank you!

79
00:05:56,000 --> 00:05:58,000
Then this isn’t the main residence?

80
00:05:58,000 --> 00:06:01,000
No. This is the butler’s quarters.

81
00:06:01,000 --> 00:06:04,000
Now please make yourselves comfortable.

82
00:06:04,000 --> 00:06:06,000
Look, thanks for the hospitality

83
00:06:07,000 --> 00:06:09,000
but we only came here to see Killua.

84
00:06:09,000 --> 00:06:11,000
So, can you take us to him?

85
00:06:11,000 --> 00:06:13,000
Like, now?

86
00:06:13,000 --> 00:06:15,000
That won’t be necessary, sir.

87
00:06:17,000 --> 00:06:20,000
Master Killua is on his way
this very moment.

88
00:06:20,000 --> 00:06:21,000
-Wait, really?
-[cups clatter]

89
00:06:22,000 --> 00:06:24,000
[Gotoh]
That’s right. So please be patient.

90
00:06:25,000 --> 00:06:27,000
-Great news, huh, Gon?
-Yep!

91
00:06:27,000 --> 00:06:28,000
[Gotoh] Now then…

92
00:06:29,000 --> 00:06:32,000
It would be so tedious
to just sit and wait.

93
00:06:32,000 --> 00:06:33,000
[smirks]

94
00:06:33,000 --> 00:06:36,000
I propose we pass the time with a game.

95
00:06:37,000 --> 00:06:38,000
Game, you say?

96
00:06:48,000 --> 00:06:50,000
Which hand holds the coin?

97
00:06:51,000 --> 00:06:52,000
[all three] The left hand.

98
00:06:54,000 --> 00:06:55,000
That is correct.

99
00:06:55,000 --> 00:06:58,000
Now I’ll move more quickly this time.

100
00:07:04,000 --> 00:07:05,000
Now. Which hand?

101
00:07:06,000 --> 00:07:08,000
It’s the left again.

102
00:07:08,000 --> 00:07:09,000
How marvelous.

103
00:07:10,000 --> 00:07:13,000
Well. I shall have to try harder
this time.

104
00:07:20,000 --> 00:07:21,000
So? Which hand?

105
00:07:23,000 --> 00:07:24,000
I’m not sure, but...

106
00:07:25,000 --> 00:07:26,000
I’d say right.

107
00:07:26,000 --> 00:07:27,000
[Gotoh] You see…

108
00:07:28,000 --> 00:07:31,000
I’ve known Master Killua his entire life

109
00:07:31,000 --> 00:07:34,000
and I care for him as I would my own son.

110
00:07:35,000 --> 00:07:36,000
In all honesty,

111
00:07:37,000 --> 00:07:40,000
I despise you for attempting
to take him away.

112
00:07:44,000 --> 00:07:45,000
Well, which hand?

113
00:07:46,000 --> 00:07:47,000
Answer.

114
00:07:48,000 --> 00:07:49,000
The left hand.

115
00:07:56,000 --> 00:07:58,000
The lady’s voice was a bare whisper.

116
00:07:59,000 --> 00:08:01,000
Her son is leaving
and it’s breaking her heart.

117
00:08:04,000 --> 00:08:05,000
I can’t forgive you.

118
00:08:07,000 --> 00:08:10,000
Before Master Killua arrives…

119
00:08:10,000 --> 00:08:13,000
I shall test each of you
by my own methods.

120
00:08:14,000 --> 00:08:15,000
You have no choice.

121
00:08:21,000 --> 00:08:22,000
Canary!

122
00:08:23,000 --> 00:08:27,000
[Gotoh] This is her punishment
for defying orders and bringing you here.

123
00:08:28,000 --> 00:08:29,000
Allow me to explain the rules.

124
00:08:30,000 --> 00:08:32,000
If you answer incorrectly you are out.

125
00:08:33,000 --> 00:08:35,000
Should you all be disqualified

126
00:08:35,000 --> 00:08:37,000
which is quite possible

127
00:08:37,000 --> 00:08:39,000
then I shall tell Master Killua
that you left.

128
00:08:40,000 --> 00:08:43,000
And that he will never see
any of you again.

129
00:08:43,000 --> 00:08:44,000
-Killua is--
-[Gotoh] Silence!

130
00:08:45,000 --> 00:08:48,000
Your very lives hang
by a most delicate thread.

131
00:08:49,000 --> 00:08:50,000
Answer my question.

132
00:08:51,000 --> 00:08:52,000
I will not ask again.

133
00:09:00,000 --> 00:09:01,000
Now, which hand?

134
00:09:04,000 --> 00:09:06,000
I couldn’t see it.

135
00:09:06,000 --> 00:09:08,000
And time is of the essence.

136
00:09:08,000 --> 00:09:10,000
You only have three seconds.

137
00:09:10,000 --> 00:09:11,000
You!

138
00:09:12,000 --> 00:09:14,000
Once three seconds have passed,
slit her throat.

139
00:09:14,000 --> 00:09:15,000
Yes, sir.

140
00:09:15,000 --> 00:09:17,000
Hold on! I pick the left hand!

141
00:09:17,000 --> 00:09:19,000
-I pick the right hand!
-Yes, me too!

142
00:09:19,000 --> 00:09:20,000
[Leorio gasps]

143
00:09:22,000 --> 00:09:23,000
[frustrated grunt]

144
00:09:24,000 --> 00:09:26,000
One has been disqualified.

145
00:09:34,000 --> 00:09:36,000
This is useless. I can’t see anything!

146
00:09:39,000 --> 00:09:40,000
Which hand?

147
00:09:42,000 --> 00:09:44,000
I choose the right hand.

148
00:09:44,000 --> 00:09:45,000
And I pick the left.

149
00:09:47,000 --> 00:09:49,000
It was in my left hand.

150
00:09:49,000 --> 00:09:51,000
Now only one remains.

151
00:09:57,000 --> 00:09:59,000
-Here we go.
-Wait just a minute!

152
00:10:01,000 --> 00:10:02,000
What is it?

153
00:10:02,000 --> 00:10:05,000
If you’re trying to buy time,
I will kill one of you.

154
00:10:05,000 --> 00:10:08,000
-Leorio! Gimme your knife.
-Huh?

155
00:10:08,000 --> 00:10:09,000
Don’t worry, okay?

156
00:10:09,000 --> 00:10:11,000
I’m not gonna use it for anything stupid.

157
00:10:19,000 --> 00:10:22,000
He cut himself to reduce the swelling…

158
00:10:26,000 --> 00:10:28,000
Dammit! How long do I have to wait?

159
00:10:29,000 --> 00:10:31,000
Hey, Gotoh!

160
00:10:33,000 --> 00:10:35,000
Is anybody out here?

161
00:10:38,000 --> 00:10:39,000
What is going on?

162
00:10:42,000 --> 00:10:44,000
There. Much better. I can see now.

163
00:10:44,000 --> 00:10:45,000
Okay, I’m ready!

164
00:10:46,000 --> 00:10:47,000
[derisive snort]

165
00:10:51,000 --> 00:10:52,000
Which hand?

166
00:10:53,000 --> 00:10:53,000
The left.

167
00:10:54,000 --> 00:10:56,000
Very good. Now…

168
00:11:07,000 --> 00:11:08,000
Now, which one of us has it?

169
00:11:12,000 --> 00:11:17,000
HUNTER GLOSSARY

170
00:11:17,000 --> 00:11:21,000
WAITING PERIOD

171
00:11:35,000 --> 00:11:37,000
That guy. Right behind me.

172
00:11:42,000 --> 00:11:43,000
[snorts]

173
00:11:43,000 --> 00:11:45,000
-[butlers applaud]
-[Gotoh] Splendid. Well done!

174
00:11:47,000 --> 00:11:49,000
Gotoh! Is Gon here yet?

175
00:11:49,000 --> 00:11:52,000
-Killua!
-You were already here? Gon!

176
00:11:52,000 --> 00:11:55,000
And this guy… um… Kurapika?

177
00:11:55,000 --> 00:11:56,000
You remembered.

178
00:11:56,000 --> 00:11:59,000
-Reolio!
-[yells] It’s Leorio!

179
00:12:00,000 --> 00:12:02,000
It’s been so long! But you made it!

180
00:12:02,000 --> 00:12:04,000
Wow! Your face is a mess!

181
00:12:05,000 --> 00:12:06,000
Back at you!

182
00:12:07,000 --> 00:12:09,000
[Gon and Killua laughing]

183
00:12:10,000 --> 00:12:14,000
Hey, Gotoh! What happened to telling me
as soon as they got here, huh?

184
00:12:14,000 --> 00:12:15,000
What were you doing?

185
00:12:16,000 --> 00:12:17,000
Please forgive me.

186
00:12:17,000 --> 00:12:20,000
I had them participate in a little game.

187
00:12:20,000 --> 00:12:21,000
A game?

188
00:12:23,000 --> 00:12:24,000
A joke, sir.

189
00:12:24,000 --> 00:12:27,000
Though quite a poor one, admittedly.

190
00:12:27,000 --> 00:12:29,000
I’m sorry for the trouble.

191
00:12:29,000 --> 00:12:32,000
I do hope you enjoyed yourselves.

192
00:12:32,000 --> 00:12:35,000
If that was a joke,
then you sure fooled me.

193
00:12:35,000 --> 00:12:36,000
Wait, did they try anything?

194
00:12:37,000 --> 00:12:39,000
No. They were just
keeping us all entertained.

195
00:12:40,000 --> 00:12:42,000
Really? Well, okay.

196
00:12:42,000 --> 00:12:45,000
Let’s go someplace else.
Like anywhere at all.

197
00:12:45,000 --> 00:12:48,000
If we stay here,
my mom will chew all of us out.

198
00:12:48,000 --> 00:12:49,000
Hm.

199
00:12:51,000 --> 00:12:53,000
Hey, Gotoh. Listen.

200
00:12:53,000 --> 00:12:56,000
No matter what Mom said, don’t follow me.

201
00:12:56,000 --> 00:12:57,000
Understood, sir.

202
00:12:57,000 --> 00:12:59,000
Please take care.

203
00:13:00,000 --> 00:13:01,000
C’mon, Gon. Let’s go.

204
00:13:02,000 --> 00:13:03,000
Bye.

205
00:13:09,000 --> 00:13:10,000
Mister Gotoh...

206
00:13:11,000 --> 00:13:14,000
You’re gonna miss Killua
when he’s gone, aren’t you?

207
00:13:15,000 --> 00:13:16,000
No, sir.

208
00:13:16,000 --> 00:13:19,000
It is our duty to serve our employers

209
00:13:19,000 --> 00:13:22,000
and not to become
emotionally attached to them.

210
00:13:23,000 --> 00:13:24,000
You liar.

211
00:13:26,000 --> 00:13:27,000
[Gotoh] Gon.

212
00:13:34,000 --> 00:13:36,000
Well? Which hand?

213
00:13:36,000 --> 00:13:37,000
Your left one, right?

214
00:13:40,000 --> 00:13:41,000
No way!

215
00:13:41,000 --> 00:13:43,000
[Gotoh] Indeed. A deception.

216
00:13:44,000 --> 00:13:47,000
The world is teeming
with tricks and tricksters.

217
00:13:50,000 --> 00:13:51,000
Please be careful.

218
00:13:52,000 --> 00:13:55,000
And please, sir, look after Master Killua.

219
00:14:01,000 --> 00:14:02,000
See ya later, Canary!

220
00:14:04,000 --> 00:14:06,000
[Killua] Hurry up, Gon!

221
00:14:06,000 --> 00:14:07,000
[Gon] Coming, sorry!

222
00:14:07,000 --> 00:14:10,000
[Killua] Let’s get out of here
before trouble finds us!

223
00:14:13,000 --> 00:14:15,000
[Killua] Yeah.
He pulled that same trick on me.

224
00:14:16,000 --> 00:14:19,000
Once you know the secret,
you’ll kick yourself for not seeing it.

225
00:14:19,000 --> 00:14:21,000
Oh. Really?

226
00:14:22,000 --> 00:14:24,000
I bet this is what he did.

227
00:14:27,000 --> 00:14:29,000
-Which hand?
-Your left, right?

228
00:14:30,000 --> 00:14:32,000
What the--?!

229
00:14:32,000 --> 00:14:33,000
But how’d ya do it?

230
00:14:34,000 --> 00:14:37,000
Gotoh must have had two coins
the entire time.

231
00:14:37,000 --> 00:14:39,000
But it looked like he only had one.

232
00:14:39,000 --> 00:14:42,000
Well he concealed a coin in his right hand

233
00:14:42,000 --> 00:14:43,000
and then he flipped the other.

234
00:14:45,000 --> 00:14:47,000
He let us see him grab the coin

235
00:14:47,000 --> 00:14:49,000
using his left hand.

236
00:14:49,000 --> 00:14:51,000
Now, this is where the skill comes in:

237
00:14:51,000 --> 00:14:54,000
Before he asked us to choose
which hand held the coin,

238
00:14:54,000 --> 00:14:56,000
he raised both of his arms like so…

239
00:14:56,000 --> 00:14:58,000
and slipped the first coin
into his sleeve,

240
00:14:59,000 --> 00:15:01,000
while keeping his hand
balled up in a fist.

241
00:15:01,000 --> 00:15:02,000
Oh!

242
00:15:03,000 --> 00:15:05,000
Then he just showed us the coin
in his right hand.

243
00:15:05,000 --> 00:15:07,000
Yep, you got it.

244
00:15:07,000 --> 00:15:09,000
[growls] That cheater!

245
00:15:09,000 --> 00:15:11,000
Well, not the whole time, probably.

246
00:15:11,000 --> 00:15:13,000
I’m sure just on the last turn.

247
00:15:13,000 --> 00:15:16,000
Gotoh hates cheating,
even if it’s just a game.

248
00:15:16,000 --> 00:15:17,000
Feel better?

249
00:15:17,000 --> 00:15:19,000
[growls] That's even worse!

250
00:15:20,000 --> 00:15:22,000
[train whistles]

251
00:15:26,000 --> 00:15:29,000
What?
Wait. You came here on a tourist visa?

252
00:15:29,000 --> 00:15:30,000
Mm-hm.

253
00:15:30,000 --> 00:15:33,000
But you passed the Hunter Exam,
didn’t you?

254
00:15:33,000 --> 00:15:35,000
So why didn’t you use your license?

255
00:15:35,000 --> 00:15:38,000
You can use it to get into other countries
and stay for as long as you want!

256
00:15:39,000 --> 00:15:40,000
We already told him that!

257
00:15:41,000 --> 00:15:42,000
Not yet. No license.

258
00:15:43,000 --> 00:15:45,000
Not until I finish what I have to do.

259
00:15:45,000 --> 00:15:47,000
So, what is it? What do you gotta do?

260
00:15:48,000 --> 00:15:50,000
Well… you remember…

261
00:15:50,000 --> 00:15:54,000
When Hisoka game me his number badge!!

262
00:15:59,000 --> 00:16:00,000
I will take it back

263
00:16:01,000 --> 00:16:04,000
but only when you can
punch me in the face like that.

264
00:16:05,000 --> 00:16:07,000
In the meantime,

265
00:16:07,000 --> 00:16:09,000
you just hold on to it for me.

266
00:16:11,000 --> 00:16:12,000
I’ll return it

267
00:16:12,000 --> 00:16:15,000
whenever I can punch Hisoka
right in his stupid, ugly face!

268
00:16:15,000 --> 00:16:19,000
Until I can do that, I’m not gonna
use my Hunter’s License

269
00:16:19,000 --> 00:16:21,000
or go back to Whale Island!

270
00:16:21,000 --> 00:16:24,000
Hmm... So? Where is Hisoka?

271
00:16:24,000 --> 00:16:24,000
Uh?

272
00:16:25,000 --> 00:16:26,000
Uh, well…

273
00:16:26,000 --> 00:16:27,000
That’s what I thought…

274
00:16:28,000 --> 00:16:30,000
I know where he is, Gon.

275
00:16:31,000 --> 00:16:32,000
Really?

276
00:16:32,000 --> 00:16:33,000
But how?

277
00:16:34,000 --> 00:16:35,000
I know because he told me.

278
00:16:37,000 --> 00:16:38,000
That’s what he said…

279
00:16:38,000 --> 00:16:39,000
[Kurapika gasps]

280
00:16:39,000 --> 00:16:40,000
[Hisoka whispers inaudibly]

281
00:16:41,000 --> 00:16:43,000
No. After the orientation.

282
00:16:44,000 --> 00:16:46,000
[Leorio] Yeah, but it’s related, right?

283
00:16:46,000 --> 00:16:47,000
Perhaps.

284
00:16:48,000 --> 00:16:50,000
Okay, look, I’ve been dying to ask.

285
00:16:50,000 --> 00:16:51,000
Hisoka…

286
00:16:51,000 --> 00:16:52,000
What did he say to you?

287
00:16:54,000 --> 00:16:56,000
All he said was…

288
00:16:57,000 --> 00:17:00,000
I’ll tell you something interesting
about spiders.

289
00:17:01,000 --> 00:17:03,000
Did he mean the Phantom Troupe?

290
00:17:03,000 --> 00:17:06,000
I don’t recall
ever mentioning them to Hisoka.

291
00:17:06,000 --> 00:17:09,000
He either overheard our conversation
during the First Phase

292
00:17:09,000 --> 00:17:11,000
or heard it from someone else.

293
00:17:12,000 --> 00:17:14,000
The troupe’s symbol is the spider

294
00:17:14,000 --> 00:17:17,000
which is what they are called
by anyone familiar with them.

295
00:17:18,000 --> 00:17:21,000
I was interested in
whatever information he had.

296
00:17:21,000 --> 00:17:23,000
I get it now.

297
00:17:23,000 --> 00:17:26,000
Okay. That actually makes sense.

298
00:17:26,000 --> 00:17:29,000
So that’s what made you swallow your pride
and take the win.

299
00:17:30,000 --> 00:17:32,000
I asked him about it
after the orientation.

300
00:17:33,000 --> 00:17:37,000
Meet me in Yorknew City
on September first.

301
00:17:38,000 --> 00:17:39,000
But why that date?

302
00:17:39,000 --> 00:17:41,000
That’s half a year away.

303
00:17:41,000 --> 00:17:43,000
You’ve got plenty of time.

304
00:17:43,000 --> 00:17:46,000
So, what’s gonna happen in Yorknew City?

305
00:17:46,000 --> 00:17:47,000
Ha!

306
00:17:47,000 --> 00:17:49,000
They’re holding
the world’s largest auction!

307
00:17:49,000 --> 00:17:50,000
That’s right.

308
00:17:50,000 --> 00:17:53,000
From September 1st
through September 10th,

309
00:17:53,000 --> 00:17:54,000
there will be an auction,

310
00:17:54,000 --> 00:17:56,000
with rare and unusual items

311
00:17:56,000 --> 00:17:59,000
and national treasures
from around the world.

312
00:17:59,000 --> 00:18:02,000
Of course, the event attracts
all manner of tricksters

313
00:18:02,000 --> 00:18:05,000
who come looking to satisfy their greed.

314
00:18:05,000 --> 00:18:08,000
It’s the biggest gathering of wealth
on the entire planet.

315
00:18:08,000 --> 00:18:10,000
Oh…

316
00:18:10,000 --> 00:18:12,000
Do you think that means
the troupe’s gonna be there?

317
00:18:12,000 --> 00:18:14,000
Well, they are a group of bandits.

318
00:18:14,000 --> 00:18:17,000
It’s unlikely that they
would let this opportunity slip by.

319
00:18:17,000 --> 00:18:19,000
Regardless...

320
00:18:19,000 --> 00:18:22,000
on that day,
Hisoka will be somewhere in Yorknew City.

321
00:18:22,000 --> 00:18:25,000
Okay, then. September the first.

322
00:18:25,000 --> 00:18:27,000
I got it. Thanks a lot!

323
00:18:34,000 --> 00:18:36,000
[Kurapika] All right. I’ll be leaving now.

324
00:18:36,000 --> 00:18:37,000
[Gon] Huh?

325
00:18:37,000 --> 00:18:39,000
We all got to see Killua again,

326
00:18:40,000 --> 00:18:41,000
so my work here is finished.

327
00:18:42,000 --> 00:18:45,000
I’ll be needing a lot of money
if I’m going to attend the auction.

328
00:18:45,000 --> 00:18:49,000
So, from here I shall search for a patron
willing to employ me as a Hunter.

329
00:18:50,000 --> 00:18:51,000
Really?

330
00:18:51,000 --> 00:18:54,000
I guess I should head back home, then.

331
00:18:54,000 --> 00:18:55,000
Wait, you too?

332
00:18:56,000 --> 00:18:58,000
I haven’t given up on becoming a doctor.

333
00:18:58,000 --> 00:19:00,000
If I’m accepted to med school,

334
00:19:00,000 --> 00:19:03,000
then this will pay
for the outrageous expenses.

335
00:19:04,000 --> 00:19:06,000
I need to get back
and start hitting the books.

336
00:19:06,000 --> 00:19:08,000
Best of luck, Leorio!

337
00:19:13,000 --> 00:19:16,000
-[Leorio] ‘Til next time…
-[Kurapika] Yes. That will be…

338
00:19:16,000 --> 00:19:19,000
[all] September first in Yorknew City!

339
00:19:20,000 --> 00:19:21,000
See ya later!

340
00:19:26,000 --> 00:19:27,000
[Gon] Bye-bye!

341
00:19:29,000 --> 00:19:31,000
Guess it’s just you and me now, Killua.

342
00:19:31,000 --> 00:19:33,000
So? What next?

343
00:19:33,000 --> 00:19:36,000
You seriously have to ask me that?
We’ve gotta start training.

344
00:19:36,000 --> 00:19:38,000
Oh. For what?

345
00:19:38,000 --> 00:19:39,000
Why not have fun?

346
00:19:39,000 --> 00:19:40,000
[Killua grunts]

347
00:19:41,000 --> 00:19:43,000
You remember what you told me
about a second ago?

348
00:19:44,000 --> 00:19:47,000
You think you can punch Hisoka in the face
without training?

349
00:19:47,000 --> 00:19:50,000
[yells] That’d take ten years!
Forget about six months!

350
00:19:53,000 --> 00:19:54,000
[Gon] Okay.

351
00:19:54,000 --> 00:19:56,000
[Killua] Here. I’ll break it down for you.

352
00:19:56,000 --> 00:19:59,000
This is Hisoka and this is Hanzo.

353
00:19:59,000 --> 00:20:00,000
[Gon] Right, I’m with you,

354
00:20:00,000 --> 00:20:03,000
[Killua] If this is the strength gap
between Hisoka and Hanzo...

355
00:20:04,000 --> 00:20:05,000
the gap between you and Hisoka is...

356
00:20:14,000 --> 00:20:17,000
[Killua] This wide!
And I’m being generous!

357
00:20:18,000 --> 00:20:19,000
[Gon] That’s just mean!

358
00:20:20,000 --> 00:20:22,000
Okay, then how far apart are you?

359
00:20:22,000 --> 00:20:23,000
[Killua] Who, me?

360
00:20:25,000 --> 00:20:27,000
Well, probably here…

361
00:20:28,000 --> 00:20:30,000
Wow! I’m so humble!

362
00:20:30,000 --> 00:20:31,000
Oh...

363
00:20:31,000 --> 00:20:33,000
So Hanzo’s the stronger one?

364
00:20:33,000 --> 00:20:34,000
Wait…

365
00:20:34,000 --> 00:20:35,000
What is it?

366
00:20:36,000 --> 00:20:38,000
[Gon] You really are awesome, Killua!

367
00:20:38,000 --> 00:20:41,000
Knock it off, all right?
It’s embarrassing.

368
00:20:41,000 --> 00:20:43,000
It’s just I don’t know
how to tell the difference in strength

369
00:20:44,000 --> 00:20:45,000
between my opponent and me.

370
00:20:45,000 --> 00:20:47,000
[Killua] It doesn’t really matter, dummy.

371
00:20:48,000 --> 00:20:49,000
I’m only estimating, anyway.

372
00:20:50,000 --> 00:20:52,000
Besides, you get the general idea, right?

373
00:20:53,000 --> 00:20:56,000
And with experience, your estimates
will become more accurate.

374
00:20:57,000 --> 00:21:00,000
But the stronger someone is,
the better they can hide that strength.

375
00:21:00,000 --> 00:21:03,000
So, it’s not a method that I’d recommend.

376
00:21:03,000 --> 00:21:04,000
Okay, I won’t.

377
00:21:04,000 --> 00:21:07,000
[Killua] Point is...
Hisoka’s really strong.

378
00:21:07,000 --> 00:21:08,000
[Gon] Yeah.

379
00:21:08,000 --> 00:21:12,000
With just six months,
we’re gonna need to get real creative.

380
00:21:12,000 --> 00:21:13,000
[grunts]

381
00:21:13,000 --> 00:21:15,000
[Killua] Hey… got any money?

382
00:21:16,000 --> 00:21:19,000
[sheepish exhale]
I’m a little low, actually.

383
00:21:19,000 --> 00:21:21,000
I don’t have much either.

384
00:21:21,000 --> 00:21:24,000
But there’s a place
where we can make ourselves some money

385
00:21:24,000 --> 00:21:26,000
and train at the same time.

386
00:21:27,000 --> 00:21:29,000
Make money while we’re training?

387
00:21:31,000 --> 00:21:32,000
At the Heavens Arena.

388
00:21:33,000 --> 00:21:35,000
Heavens Arena?

389
00:21:35,000 --> 00:21:37,000
Yeah! I’ll explain later.

390
00:21:37,000 --> 00:21:39,000
But we really ought to get going now!

391
00:21:40,000 --> 00:21:41,000
[Gon] Right!

392
00:21:45,000 --> 00:21:48,000
[narrator] After bidding farewell
to Kurapika and Leorio,

393
00:21:48,000 --> 00:21:51,000
as well as promising to meet again
in Yorknew City,

394
00:21:51,000 --> 00:21:54,000
Gon and Killua move on to a new stage:

395
00:21:54,000 --> 00:21:56,000
the Heavens Arena.

396
00:21:57,000 --> 00:21:59,000
[theme song playing]

397
00:23:21,000 --> 00:23:24,000
[Gon] Next time: “Then x And x After”!

398
00:23:24,000 --> 00:23:25,000
Sweet and spicy!

399
00:23:25,000 --> 00:23:26,000
[Mito] Salty and spicy!

400
00:23:26,000 --> 00:23:28,000
[Gon] Spicy is good for you!
